 ("Keep GEO within sound SEO practice","Google says its AI search features use the same foundational SEO requirements and that there are no extra technical eligibility requirements. Good GEO therefore builds on crawlability, useful people-first content, internal links, a good page experience and structured data that matches visible content—not special schema or guaranteed placement."),
 ("Track a repeatable sample, not a promise","Answer outputs change across prompts, users and time. We record a dated prompt set and the platform tested, then report mentions, cited pages and context as directional observations. Search Console and analytics may help identify visits and conversions, but do not necessarily isolate every AI feature."),
