# Results page (no fabricated case studies)
results_content=f'''<section class="section"><div class="container measurement-page"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">A CLEAR VIEW OF PROGRESS</p><h2>Measure the work. Understand the limits. Decide what comes next.</h2><p class="lead">ClearPath agrees useful measures before work begins, then reports what changed in plain language. No unverified client numbers or outcome guarantees.</p></div><div class="measurement-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Set a baseline</h3><p>Review the available website, advertising, search and enquiry data. Record gaps before comparing periods.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Define meaningful actions</h3><p>Agree what counts as an enquiry, a qualified opportunity or another useful action for your business.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Review evidence together</h3><p>Separate measured activity from lead quality and revenue. Include sales-team feedback where available.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Choose the next step</h3><p>Explain what is working, what remains uncertain and which test or improvement should happen next.</p></article></div><div class="prose results-method"><h2>What reporting can—and cannot—show</h2><p>We can report agreed events such as calls, form submissions, campaign spend, search visibility and page engagement when the relevant measurement is available and configured. We do not present platform-reported conversions as a complete account of business impact.</p><p>Attribution is imperfect: customers may see an ad, return later through search or call from another device. We document tracking changes, identify data limitations and avoid claiming that a channel caused revenue when the evidence does not support that conclusion. ClearPath does not publish client outcomes without verification and permission.</p></div><a class="button button-primary" href="/contact/">Talk through your goals {svg('arrow')}</a></div></section>'''
OUT.joinpath("results").mkdir(exist_ok=True)
OUT.joinpath("results/index.html").write_text(page("Measurement & Reporting | ClearPath","Learn how ClearPath establishes baselines, defines useful enquiries, reports marketing activity and explains attribution limits.","Measure the work. Understand the limits. Decide what comes next.","/results/","Measurement",results_content,"marketing measurement and reporting"),encoding="utf-8")

